11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The film is about the Tuskegee Airmen, a group of African-American United
States Army Air Forces (USAAF) servicemen during World War II.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The characters in the film are fictional, although based on real individuals.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film was produced by Lucasfilm Ltd.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
and released by 20th Century Fox, and would be the last film Lucasfilm released
before being purchased by The Walt Disney Company nine months later.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
This was Cuba Gooding Jr.'s first theatrically released film in five
years since his starring role in 2007's Daddy Day Camp.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
John Ridley wrote the screenplay.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Additional material was shot the following year with executive producer George
Lucas as director and Aaron McGruder as writer of the reshoots.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It was filmed in March and July 2009.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Red Tails was a personal project for Lucas, one that
he had originally conceived in 1988.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
It is the first Lucasfilm production since the 1994 film Radioland Murders that
is not associated with the Indiana Jones or Star Wars franchises.

